Fix: use the GTSAM pose optimizer in the frontend, not g2o

The C++ core's g2o pose optimizer is a no-op on this build. Reproduced in upstream's
own unit test (pyslam/slam/cpp/tests_py/test_slam_cpp_optimize_pose.py) on synthetic
data with correct intrinsics:

    g2o   : R diff 0.4129, t diff 0.5196, RMSE 156.3355750 -> 156.3355750  (FAIL)
    GTSAM : R diff 0.000303, t diff 0.000959, RMSE 156.3355750 -> 0.6816   (OK)

RMSE bit-identical before/after proves g2o never updates the frame pose. In the live
pipeline this made every reprojection error stay huge, so pose optimization flagged
100% of points as outliers ("available 54 points, found 54 bad points"), matched map
points fell to 0, and tracking failed and reset 152 times over KITTI 06.

kOptimizationFrontEndUseGtsam was False, selecting the broken g2o path. GTSAM is built
and verified working here, so switch the frontend to it.

Scope: frontend pose optimization only. kOptimizationBundleAdjustUseGtsam and
kOptimizationLoopClosingUseGtsam are left False -- those g2o paths are untested here
and should be changed only on evidence.

Not investigated: WHY the statically-linked g2o is inert (1133 g2o symbols are present
in cpp_core.so, so it is not a linkage failure). Left alone because GTSAM works.

Upstream: luigifreda/pyslam master @ a5ff256 (no release tags exist).
